===Etymology 1===
From {{etyl|non|en}} {{term|skriða||[[landslip]]|lang=non}}. Also see [[screed]].

====Noun====
{{en-noun|s|-}}

# {{uncountable}} loose [[stony]] [[debris]] on a slope
# a slope of such material at the base of a [[cliff]], etc

====Verb====
{{en-verb|screes|screeing|screed}}

# {{rfv-sense}} to flatten or level [[concrete]], while still wet, and clear protruding stones and gravel from the surface
#*{{title=Roof gardens: history, design, and construction‎|page=196|author=Theodore Osmundson|year=1999|passage=The sand bed is screed in preparation for laying the precast paving}}
# To traverse [[scree#Noun|scree]].

